  "cues": [
   [
    0.12,
    "But a treaty was hard to agree."
   ],
   [
    2.061,
    "Ozone loss affects every country, so a treaty would only work if it was global."
   ],
   [
    7.473,
    "And countries wanted different things."
   ],
   [
    9.641,
    "Developing countries feared that limits on these chemicals could hold back their industrial growth."
   ],
   [
    15.346,
    "Countries whose industries relied heavily on them, like those of the European Union, worried about the cost."
   ],
   [
    22.234,
    "Some argued that the harm had not been proven yet."
   ],
   [
    25.306,
    "And countries that had already cut their own C F C use, like the United States, Canada, Sweden and Norway, didn't want others to keep using them."
   ],
   [
    35.04,
    "All of these interests had to meet at one table."
   ]
  ]
